NAME
    touch - create empty files

SYNOPSIS
    touch name [name ...]

DESCRIPTION
    Makes each name that does not exist yet a 0-byte file, with no
    load address. An existing file or directory is left alone: it is
    not truncated, and Y1/OS keeps no timestamps to update. Names may
    be relative or absolute. "touch: cannot create NAME" when the
    directory is missing or the name is not valid. touch is /BIN/TOUCH.

LIMITS
    No globs (a pattern could only match files that already exist).
    Names are 1..12 characters.

EXAMPLES
    touch /NEW.TXT
    touch A.TXT B.TXT /T/C.TXT

NOTES
    Removed from the P8X version: the /d1 mount.
    Ported from P8X os/commands/touch.c 2026-09-23.

